@startuml menu-flow
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Menu → Single Player / Tutorial / Review replay

actor Player

package "apps/starchess" {
  component "StarChessMenuRoute\n/ (Router base /starchess)" as MENU <<app>>
  component "StarChessMenuScreen\n+ MenuSky / MenuArrival" as UI <<app>>
  component "ChessMenuMockup\nglass · shatter SVGs" as MOCK <<async>>
  component "NewGamePanel\nMAP · TEAM · OPPONENT · START" as SETUP <<app>>
  component "navigate /single?map=&team=&opponent=" as NAV <<async>>
  component "navigate /tutorial" as NAVT <<async>>
  component "navigate /review" as NAVR <<async>>
  component "SingleScreen\nopponent admission" as ADMIT <<app>>
  component "SingleScreen\nUnavailable · Not implemented\nno live match for known placeholder\nfrom URL or session" as UNAVAILABLE <<error>>
  component "StarChessSingleScreen\nMatchStore + LiveMatchShell\nStarChessScreen turnChrome=sidebar\nAdjutant = opposite of team\nscript = ?opponent (naive|strategic)" as LIVE <<app>>
  component "StarChessTutorialScreen\n/tutorial/:section/:story\n(TUTORIAL_SCRIPT ids)\nKerrigan header · HOME-only\ne.g. /tutorial/fog/king" as TUT <<app>>
  component "TutorialCompleteConfirm\nlive-play-attack-3 enemy HP=0\nwhen tutorialCleared=false" as TUTDONE <<app>>
  component "localStorage\nstarchess_tutorial_cleared" as TUTFLAG <<db>>
  component "ExitGameConfirm\nHome during planning/targeting/resolving" as EXIT <<error>>
  component "gameOver → matchHistory\nMatchResultModal\nVICTORY|DEFEAT (+DRAW)" as END <<db>>
  component "MatchResultModal\nAnother Game · Replay" as RESULT <<app>>
  component "StarChessReviewScreen\n/review list · /review/:id DualNav" as REV <<app>>
}

Player ARROW_MAIN MENU
MENU ARROW_MAIN UI
UI ARROW_OPTIONAL MOCK : from /chess/\n(session flag)
MOCK ARROW_MAIN UI : glass · Kerrigan\n· shatter · chrome in
UI ARROW_MAIN SETUP : Single Player
SETUP ARROW_MAIN NAV : START
NAV ARROW_MAIN ADMIT
ADMIT ARROW_MAIN LIVE : naive | strategic
ADMIT ARROW_ERROR UNAVAILABLE : machine-learning | rlhf | rlcd
UI ARROW_MAIN NAVT : Tutorial
NAVT ARROW_MAIN TUT
UI ARROW_MAIN NAVR : Review
NAVR ARROW_MAIN REV
LIVE ARROW_ERROR EXIT : Home
EXIT ARROW_OPTIONAL MENU : Leave confirmed
TUT ARROW_OPTIONAL MENU : Home
TUT ARROW_MAIN TUTDONE : live-play-attack-3 win\n+ uncleared
TUTDONE ARROW_MAIN TUTFLAG : Go Home → cleared=true
TUTDONE ARROW_MAIN MENU : Go Home
LIVE ARROW_MAIN END : gameOver
END ARROW_MAIN RESULT : save + open modal
RESULT ARROW_MAIN LIVE : Another Game\n(same map+team rematch)
RESULT ARROW_MAIN REV : Replay\nreplace /review/:id

note bottom of SETUP
  Core catalog owns IDs and labels.
  Only naive and strategic remain playable.
  EMPTY definitions do not implement players.
end note

note right of SETUP
  Setup restores the last playable choice from
  starchess_setup rather than resetting it.
  Coach difficulty uses a separate settings key,
  so it cannot select an Adjutant opponent.
end note

note bottom of ADMIT
  A recognized URL opponent wins over a session;
  unknown or missing values retain legacy resume.
  A known EMPTY definition stays unavailable,
  so it cannot silently launch a naive match.
end note

note bottom of LIVE
  Naive: engine rules only.
  Strategic: rules, vision, and tactics.
end note

note right of LIVE
  The screen folds ccIntel and kvs once per turn
  through core tracking, as the arena does.
  Shared folds accumulate the CC posterior
  consistently across live and headless play.
end note

note left of LIVE
  Resume stores an optional opponent in v: 1;
  legacy blobs without it mean naive.
  An opponent mismatch prevents resume because
  changing the script would create another game.
end note

note bottom of END
  An optional record opponent names the script,
  while legacy records retain the plain
  Adjutant label. Imported arenaPlayers takes
  precedence over that field because it
  identifies both sides of the matchup.
end note

note bottom of RESULT
  Another Game preserves map, team, opponent.
  Replay replaces the route with /review/:id.
  Results: VICTORY / DEFEAT / DRAW.
end note

note bottom of REV
  /review: Blue/Red + date pages; Back only.
  No First move filter or Review title.
  useMatchHistoryFilters owns the filters.
end note

note right of REV
  Dynamic MobileBanner exclusively owns Back
  and compact swatches plus date paging,
  with no caption. The in-flow inset disappears
  because its minimum content height collides
  with the list.
end note

note left of REV
  /review/:id: Coach-style title stack
  above ReviewTurnNav, e.g. Win (Blue) and
  Alex (Blue) vs Adjutant (Red).
  MobileBanner link: href=/.
end note

note bottom of UI
  Multiplayer MenuAnchor: disabled.
  Label: Coming Soon.
end note

note bottom of MOCK
  StarChessRedirect sets starchess_from_chess
  on the nerd-approved /chess/ → /starchess/ hop.
  MenuArrival then plays the mockup transition.
end note

note right of MOCK
  Coach data-theme: light/dark tokens.
  Glass → sky; Selena → Kerrigan.
  Buttons shatter; StarChess anchors fade in.
  Storybook: Screens/Menu, toggle, Theme toolbar.
end note

note left of MOCK
  Match Coach MenuScreen box-for-box.
  Desktop/dynamic: two columns; portrait: one.
  Include sub-480 root-font scaling
  and the dynamic-band chat bubble.
end note

note as SHORTCUT
  Play StarChess: under fused Play, column 1.
  Style token: --sc-menu-neon.
end note
MOCK .. SHORTCUT

note as NERD_FLAG
  The mockup reads store/nerdFlag once without
  modifying the value because Coach owns that
  persisted setting. Coach sets it before
  navigation, so the arriving menu needs
  no subscription.
end note
SHORTCUT .. NERD_FLAG

note bottom of TUT
  IDs come from TUTORIAL_SCRIPT.
  /tutorial defaults to the first Fog story.
  Examples: /tutorial/fog/king and
  /tutorial/specials/marine.
end note

note right of TUT
  One hints step wins per beat: first matching
  when, otherwise the unconditional entry.
  Squares mark destinations; arrows join squares.
end note

note as HINTS
  Arrows paint above the fog overlay because
  a tutorial may cross squares outside the
  player's vision. They remain presentational
  rather than validating a legal or
  unobstructed board move.
end note
TUT .. HINTS

note as HINT_EXAMPLES
  live-play-attack-1: h1-a8 x-ray.
  Ship hint: d8-a8 shot.
end note
HINTS .. HINT_EXAMPLES

note as LESSON_LOOP
  Objective → ending → success → next.
  Goal text lives only in the coach bubble.
  completeWhen / restartWhen: settled board only.
  Timeline must be idle when judging either.
end note
TUT .. LESSON_LOOP

note as ENDING
  Preserve the closing message in the ending
  state for its required reading interval
  before success. The success bubble suppresses
  that message, so an immediate transition
  would discard the lesson's conclusion.
end note
LESSON_LOOP .. ENDING

note as READING_TIME
  lessonEndMessageMs: approximately 200 wpm.
  Floor 1.2s; ceiling 4s; no line means no hold.
end note
ENDING .. READING_TIME

note as SUCCESS
  Success: Objective complete + Next lesson.
  Suppress the message between those labels.
  LESSON_ADVANCE_MS: 3s, drawn on CTA border.
  CTA skips wait; Retry preserves failure line.
end note
ENDING .. SUCCESS

note as COMPLETION_GUARD
  Every live lesson requires completeWhen
  because an unchecked objective is a dead end.
  The tutorialLessons test guards this contract
  rather than relying on manual progression.
end note
SUCCESS .. COMPLETION_GUARD

note as OBSERVER
  Stage 3: combat-chain (COMBAT_HISTORY),
  then king-hunt (KING_HISTORY).
  Story keys remount the timeline.
  Stage 4 uses live boards only.
end note
TUT .. OBSERVER

note as PHASE_NAV
  Stage 3 uses Review Back + ReviewTurnNav,
  with turn/phase in the rail and hideDualNav.
  Arrows step Check → Intent → Resolve phases.
  Phase readout replaces TutorialTypewriterNav.
end note
OBSERVER .. PHASE_NAV

note as SLOW_REVIEW
  playReviewTurn resolves an entire turn
  without intermediate phase stops.
  The lesson instead presents each phase
  separately, providing a slower introduction
  to the Review screen.
end note
PHASE_NAV .. SLOW_REVIEW

note bottom of TUTDONE
  starchess_tutorial_cleared defaults false.
  King Attack #3: enemy HP=0 while uncleared
  opens TutorialCompleteConfirm.
  Go Home writes cleared=true and returns home.
end note

note bottom of EXIT
  Live/tutorial top-panel leave chrome:
  ScreenBackNav + ChevronNav, with Back.
  Labeled panels also use PanelTitle.
end note
@enduml
